invariant: INV-14
file: quic_token.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh quic_token
reason: the check stops bounding the Original Destination Connection ID's
  length, so a token whose tag verifies and whose first length byte is above
  CH_QUIC_DCID_MAX is copied into the 20-byte array *cids gives it and
  writes past its end. Only a holder of the key can make such a token, so
  no minted token in a test shows it. The quic_token harness drives the
  check over every length byte with the tag unconstrained, and its memcpy
  bounds check fails. Each run is a proof of about a minute, so this
  belongs to the nightly's test-invariants-proof-backed job.

--- old
    if (r.err || rb_left(&r) != 0 || original_dcid_len > CH_QUIC_DCID_MAX ||
        retry_scid_len > CH_QUIC_DCID_MAX) {
--- new
    if (r.err || rb_left(&r) != 0 || retry_scid_len > CH_QUIC_DCID_MAX) {
